<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia</h1><p class="st-meta">1939 CE – 1945 CE · capital Prague</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nazi-occupied Czech lands, nominally autonomous but ruled through terror, deportations and forced labour from 1939 to 1945.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a> and the loss of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetenland">Sudetenland</a> in 1938, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied the rest of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Moravia</a> on 15 March 1939, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> declared independence. The next day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Hitler</a> proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-castle">Prague Castle</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A Czech government under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emil-hacha">Emil Hácha</a> remained in place, but real power lay with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-protector">Reich Protector</a>, first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-neurath">Konstantin von Neurath</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a>. Czech universities were closed in 1939, and Czech industry, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skoda">Škoda</a> works, served the German war effort. Heydrich was assassinated by Czech parachutists in 1942, and the Nazis destroyed the villages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lidice">Lidice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezaky">Ležáky</a> in reprisal. Most Czech <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were deported via <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theresienstadt-ghetto">Theresienstadt</a> and murdered.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> uprising broke out on 5 May 1945, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> entered Prague on 9 May. The territory was restored to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, which expelled most of its German population in the following two years.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/protectorate-of-bohemia-and-moravia.jpg" alt="Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Protectorate_of_Bohemia_and_Moravia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1939 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Prague</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Emil Hácha, Konstantin von Neurath, Reinhard Heydrich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Czech, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Protektorat Böhmen und Mähren</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1942&amp;focus=protectorate-of-bohemia-and-moravia" aria-label="Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5010 436 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5330 692L5300 622M5330 692L5330 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5300 622h0M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5330 692h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Prague. <a href="/atlas?year=1942&amp;focus=protectorate-of-bohemia-and-moravia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
